From c88a692e989c391d2c8478f0f7c2069d21d6f25b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <root@your.mom>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 17:26:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fuse selected-logit gather, FP32 conversion and masking in
 TileLang

Upstream-base: local-inference-lab/vllm 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354 plus candidate-38 source 1f33102547e4da5c64712390604695d1abd577c4.

Rationale: raw_logits and processed_logits still launch ATen gather, cast and mask kernels. Emit selected FP32 values in one TileLang store and declare all dtype, id-type and masking variants before the cache freezes.

Quality: preserve selected logits, signed zeros, infinities, NaNs, token ranks and score ordering; invalid custom-id columns stay negative infinity and are not dereferenced. No change to sampling or log-softmax arithmetic.

Tests: extend selected-score GPU coverage for dtype/stride/mask contracts, CUDA graphs and frozen-cache warmup; exercise prompt chunks, speculative chunks, custom ids and all score modes. Native qualification and benchmark receipts belong to the deployment experiment.

Upstream-status: local candidate, not submitted upstream.
